{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Atone for Your people.</b> They expounded in the Pesikta: ״כפר לעמך״ — these are the living, who achieve atonement through their money; ״אשר פדית״ — these are the dead, who achieve atonement through the money of the living. From this we learn that the consecrations which the living practice by consecrating them on behalf of the dead bring benefit to the dead, and all the more so if the son consecrates on behalf of his father — it is a merit for his father, since the son consumes its fruits; and the same applies to one who says Kaddish on his behalf or recites some blessing in the synagogue in public, as they said in the Aggadah in that story of Rabbi Akiva, as found in tractate Kallah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:46.964724702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}